      "direction": "monolith_slab",
      "name": "Monolith Slab Slim Detector",
      "form_language": "Chamfered-slab monolith: a single extruded-looking body with a continuous 2.5 mm 45\u00b0 chamfer band around the entire perimeter that reads as one machined plane; no parting-line ornamentation, no raised bezels, no logos on the front. The front face is a flat uninterrupted field carrying only the display window, which is flush-glazed and inset 0.3 mm to sit optically below the surface. The top edge becomes the air-handling datum: the intake grille is a single centred slot array recessed 1.2 mm into the chamfer so it is visually part of the form rather than applied. The bottom edge carries the USB-C port in a small chamfered cut-out, keeping the front and top planes clean. Wall stock is a uniform 1.5 mm with local ribs, giving a stiff, dense, premium feel at a slim 25.5 mm overall height.",
